  "summary": "Malicious code in melcuratts (PyPI)",
  "details": "\n---\n_-= Per source details. Do not edit below this line.=-_\n\n## Source: amazon-inspector (01116dad2488eeeb0e57fc2ae314e507b8cb8aad04245f54ddb89eb2f019441e)\nmelcuratts 0.1.0 contains no observed install-time or import-time execution of attacker-controlled code, no credential or environment harvesting, no outbound network to attacker-controlled destinations, no silent relay of caller-supplied data, no persistence or backdoor mechanism, and no shipped third-party credentials. No supply-chain attack fingerprint is present in the package contents.\n\n## Source: kam193 (8bd7e6eda0ded5ef0e82eac489faca560422a8b8e46fd9c8d9b8215d9e89e6ba)\nThis campaign consists of similar loader packages, which provide executing code from a given URL. While they do not contain the malicious payload and the usage remains unknown, they are clearly a coordinated campaign to place multiple deceptive ways to load malicious code.\n\n\n---\n\nCategory: MALICIOUS - The campaign has clearly malicious intent, like infostealers.\n\n\nCampaign: 2026-10-voice-synthesis-profiles\n\n\nReasons (based on the campaign):\n\n\n - Downloads and executes a remote malicious script.\n\n\n - other\n",
